From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pulse: declare nanosleep and errno explicitly

License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: downstream-only
Origin: openEuler RISC-V packaging

The 1.2.0 PulseAudio driver calls nanosleep and checks errno without directly
including their declaring headers. The hardened riscv64 compiler rejects the
implicit declaration. Add the POSIX headers without changing the driver or
disabling the plugin. Remove this patch when upstream includes them.

---
 src/plugins/pulse/ao_pulse.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/plugins/pulse/ao_pulse.c b/src/plugins/pulse/ao_pulse.c
--- a/src/plugins/pulse/ao_pulse.c
+++ b/src/plugins/pulse/ao_pulse.c
@@ -33 +33,3 @@
-#include <limits.h>
+#include <limits.h>
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <time.h>
